{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/pulls/189686","id":4081580672,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAeUeuM7zR_qA","html_url":"https://github.com/flutter/flutter/pull/189686","diff_url":"https://github.com/flutter/flutter/pull/189686.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/flutter/flutter/pull/189686.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/issues/189686","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/pulls/189686/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/pulls/189686/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/issues/189686/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/statuses/8e1036c014318ddd8d46defb0bf744d6d01f4628","number":189686,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[iOS] Preserve semantics parents after reparenting","user":{"login":"AfzalivE","id":436057,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNjA1Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/436057?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE","html_url":"https://github.com/AfzalivE","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AfzalivE/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/100946.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nReordering a `ReorderableListView` on iOS could move VoiceOver focus to the upper-left corner of the screen. The affected items could no longer be focused at their visual positions.\r\n\r\nDuring a reorder, semantics children move through temporary containers used by the drag overlay and drop animation. A child may already have been attached to its replacement `SemanticsObject` when its previous parent is updated or deallocated.\r\n\r\nThe previous parent unconditionally cleared the child's `parent` property. This overwrote the new parent relationship and disconnected the child from the native semantics hierarchy.\r\n\r\n`SemanticsObject` calculates its global accessibility frame by walking this parent chain and composing each ancestor's transform. Once the chain was disconnected, the element retained only its local physical-pixel rectangle. On a 3x simulator, the expected frame:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{{0, 286}, {402, 56}}\r\n```\r\n\r\nbecame:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{{0, 0}, {134, 18.67}}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis accounts for both the missing translation and the frame being reduced by the device pixel ratio.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nOnly clear a child's parent when the `SemanticsObject` performing cleanup still owns that parent relationship:\r\n\r\n```objc\r\nchild.parent == self\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis guard is applied when:\r\n\r\n- A `SemanticsObject` is deallocated.\r\n- Its traversal-order children are replaced.\r\n- Its hit-test-order children are replaced.\r\n\r\nA previous parent can now release its stale child references without detaching a child that has already moved under a replacement container. The complete ancestor transform remains available when calculating the native accessibility frame.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nAdded An iOS XCUITest that performs the default mobile long-press reorder gesture, verifies the resulting native semantic traversal order, and asserts that the reordered item retains the expected accessibility frame.\r\n\r\nThe integration app also includes a deterministic direct-drag fixture for exercising XCUITest drag synthesis.\r\n\r\nValidation performed:\r\n\r\n- `testReorderableListAccessibilityHierarchyUpdates` passes with the locally built engine.\r\n- `packages/flutter/test/widgets/reorderable_list_test.dart` passes.\r\n- `packages/flutter/test/material/reorderable_list_test.dart` passes.\r\n- `ios_test_flutter` builds successfully.\r\n- Engine formatting and Dart analysis pass.\r\n\r\n## Pre-launch Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I read the [Contributor Guide] and followed the process outlined there for submitting PRs.\r\n- [x] I read the [AI contribution guidelines] and understand my responsibilities, or I am not using AI tools.\r\n- [x] I read the [Tree Hygiene] wiki page, which explains my responsibilities.\r\n- [x] I read and followed the [Flutter Style Guide], including [Features we expect every widget to implement].\r\n- [x] I signed the [CLA].\r\n- [x] I listed at least one issue that this PR fixes in the description above.\r\n- [x] I updated/added relevant documentation (doc comments with `///`).\r\n- [x] I added new tests to check the change I am making, or this PR is [test-exempt].\r\n- [x] I followed the [breaking change policy] and added [Data Driven Fixes] where supported.\r\n- [ ] All existing and new tests are passing.\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":283479936,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM0Nzk5MzY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/labels/platform-ios","name":"platform-ios","description":"iOS applications specifically","color":"c0408a","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":284438921,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODQ0Mzg5MjE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/labels/engine","name":"engine","description":"flutter/engine related. See also e: labels.","color":"FC6401","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":323742511,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjM3NDI1MTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/labels/a:%20accessibility","name":"a: accessibility","description":"Accessibility, e.g. VoiceOver or TalkBack. (aka a11y)","color":"55ddbb","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5706368542,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAeUeuM8AAAABVCBGHg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/labels/team-ios","name":"team-ios","description":"Owned by iOS platform team","color":"198022","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10404216443,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAeUeuM8AAAACbCO-ew","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flutter/flutter/labels/CICD","name":"CICD","description":"Run CI/CD","color":"0052cc","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-18T07:43:20Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T22:35:58Z","closed_at":"2026-09-01T19:39:38Z","merged_at":"2026-09-01T19:39:38Z","merge_commit_sha":"03ebdcd6bd92a06081e2f24fff97f0ba6dbe731d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"cbracken","id":351029,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTAyOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken","html_url":"https://github.com/cbracken","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cbracken/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"AfzalivE:afzal/fix-100946","ref":"afzal/fix-100946","repo":{"id":92215793,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk5MjIxNTc5Mw=="